-- title:
--   Original Gaussian strictly positive stopped reward dominated by an initially centred L1 residual
-- statement:
--   For the genuine zero-jump original Levy process X and original admissible capped dividend control D, every original right-continuous ruin-bounded stopping clock has one integrable source martingale residual, conditionally centred on the original time-zero right-continuous filtration, dominating the exact strictly prepayment positive-clock discounted terminal plus strict-before-stop Stieltjes dividend cash. This is the physical C2 Ito-Stieltjes source certificate needed by source event theorem 642de490; the latter follows using already-Proved initial event measurability and original bounded-terminal/strict-cash L1 results, with no replacement filtration or changed ruin conventions. The certificate requires establishing the actual stochastic Ito/Taylor/compensator limit at the final clipped cell; no expectation bound is assumed.
-- source:
--   Source-exact necessary reduction child for original finite Gaussian positive clock 642de490. The physical martingale domination is strictly stronger than its initial-event expected upper. No circular import from c31f81c8/d1caa4aa/47a4991e.

